---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const netlifyForms = site.quoteForm.netlify && !site.quoteEndpoint;
---

<Layout
  title="Website Privacy"
  description="How the Utopia Logistics website handles information when you prepare and send a freight quote request, download a copy, or follow a map link."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title={'Your information.\nYour next enquiry.'}
    description="A plain-language explanation of how this website handles the details you choose to share."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container privacy-content">
      <section>
        <h2>Preparing a quote request</h2>
        <p>
          The quote form asks for your name, company, and email address, your
          pickup and delivery locations, and a description of the freight it
          concerns. Phone, province or state, postal or ZIP code, pallet or
          package count, dimensions, weight, stackability, equipment requests,
          dates, location requirements, and additional notes are optional. These
          details describe the shipment you want to discuss.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing leaves your browser while you fill the form in. Your entries
          are shown back to you on a review screen first, and are transmitted
          only when you choose to send the request. Entries are not saved in
          browser storage, so refreshing or leaving the page may clear them.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Where your request goes</h2>
        {netlifyForms ? (
          <>
            <p>
              This website is hosted on Netlify, and quote requests are
              delivered by Netlify Forms. When you send a request, the details
              you entered are transmitted to Netlify, Inc., which stores the
              submission and makes it available to Utopia Logistics dispatch.
              Netlify also records technical information such as your IP address
              and the time of submission, and applies automated spam filtering.
              That filtering includes a hidden field the form asks you to leave
              empty; genuine submissions are unaffected by it.
            </p>
            <p>
              Netlify is based in the United States, so your request is
              processed and stored outside Canada. Netlify acts as our service
              provider for handling these submissions. Their handling of the
              data is described in the{' '}
              <a
                href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Netlify privacy policy
              </a>
              .
            </p>
            <p>
              Utopia Logistics uses these details to respond to your enquiry and
              discuss the shipment. Contact dispatch if you want to correct a
              request, ask for it to be deleted, or confirm that it arrived.
            </p>
          </>
        ) : site.quoteEndpoint ? (
          <p>
            When you send the form, your information is transmitted to the
            connected enquiry service for processing. Its response page provides
            the submission result. Contact dispatch if you need to verify that
            your enquiry was received.
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            Preparing and reviewing a request happens in your browser. The
            website does not send those form details to dispatch automatically.
          </p>
        )}
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Downloads, email, and phone</h2>
        <p>
          The review screen offers a copy of your request as a text file saved
          by your browser. That download happens on your device, and you control
          where you keep or share it.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you email or call dispatch instead of using the form, the
          information is handled through the email and telephone services used
          by you and Utopia Logistics rather than through this website.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Links and website resources</h2>
        <p>
          The site’s fonts, photographs, and map illustration are served as part
          of the website. No advertising trackers, analytics scripts, or
          embedded third-party maps have been added to this build.
        </p>
        <p>
          Choosing “Get directions” opens Google Maps. That service handles
          information according to its own privacy practices. Phone and email
          links open the relevant app on your device. Website hosting and
          network providers may process technical request information needed to
          serve the site.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Questions about your information</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about information you have shared with Utopia Logistics,
          including an enquiry you want to correct or discuss, contact{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or{' '}
          <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>. Include enough context for
          the team to identify your enquiry.
        </p>
        <address>
          {site.name}
          <br />
          {site.street}
          <br />
          {site.locality}
          <br />
          Canada
        </address>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .privacy-content {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .privacy-content > section + section {
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 35px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .privacy-content h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 550;
    letter-spacing: -0.7px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .privacy-content p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.95;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .privacy-content a {
    color: var(--blue);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .privacy-content address {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.9;
    margin-top: 23px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .privacy-content h2 {
      font-size: 24px;
    }
    .privacy-content p {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
  }
</style>
